  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Tripling NHS investment by 2008 with maximum 18-week waits; major public health actions (smoking restrictions, nutrition standards, curb junk food ads); halving child poverty via tax credits, childcare and Sure Start; extended maternity leave and childcare support; raise minimum wage; expand social housing and free off-peak bus travel; strong anti-discrimination agenda and a Single Equality Act; neighborhood policing, tougher sentences, and counter-terror measures; retain independent nuclear deterrent and support veterans; ambitious climate targets (−60% CO2 by 2050) and universal kerbside recycling. TEXT_G: Leave the EU and regain legal primacy; near-zero net immigration with strict asylum rules; increase defense spending and disengage from EU defense structures; strong law-and-order stance with more prisons and homeowner protections; NHS decentralization and consideration of private insurance; sweeping deregulation and significant tax cuts; repeal the Human Rights Act; restrict GM crops and emphasize domestic control of environmental policy.",
  "reasoning": "Care is the electorate’s highest value, with moderate concern for Authority, Loyalty, and Equality. TEXT_E prioritizes healthcare, poverty reduction, family support and anti-discrimination while still reinforcing policing and national defense, whereas TEXT_G concentrates on sovereignty, immigration control and deregulation with relatively less emphasis on welfare and equality, so TEXT_E better matches the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
